{"Title":"An Act to amend the general officer designation in the state staff of the militia","BillNumber":"H3529","DocketNumber":"HD2622","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"ERP1","Name":"Edward R. Philips","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/ERP1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T15:16:34.247"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"ERP1","Name":"Edward R. Philips","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/ERP1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T15:16:34.2466667"},{"Id":"BJA1","Name":"Bruce J. Ayers","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BJA1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T15:06:23.2833333"},{"Id":"JRO0","Name":"Jacob R. Oliveira","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JRO0","ResponseDate":"2023-04-21T15:18:41.24"},{"Id":"N_C0","Name":"Nick Collins","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/N_C0","ResponseDate":"2023-10-25T12:57:37.2233333"}],"JointSponsor":{"Id":"BJA1","Name":"Bruce J. Ayers","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BJA1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T12:33:27.473"},"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3529/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representatives Philips of Sharon and Ayers of Quincy, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3529) of Edward R. Philips and Bruce J. Ayers relative to the general officer designation in the state staff of the militia.  Veterans and Federal Affairs.","DocumentText":"\tChapter 33 of the General Laws is hereby amended by inserting, in Section 15(a), in line 3, by adding after the word “general.” the following:\r\n\t“The adjutant general shall be the commanding general of all military forces, organized militia units, and the military division of the Commonwealth.”\r\n\tAnd by striking, in Section 15(b), the following: “provided, however, that the adjutant general shall not personally exercise command of troops.”\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J31","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J31"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}